From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Martin Lund <mrlund@hotmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 11:40:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 35/66] ASoC: codecs: aw882308: unmute from trigger, after BCLK
 is running

On 7.3 q6apm-lpass-dais starts the back-end graph in .trigger, no
longer in .prepare. The amplifier start in .mute_stream ran at the end
of prepare, before BCLK, and its PLL never locked (SYSST 0x0020,
NOCLKS; start failed, -110). Use mute_unmute_on_trigger so the start
runs after the CPU DAI trigger has started the graph.
---
 sound/soc/codecs/aw882308.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/aw882308.c b/sound/soc/codecs/aw882308.c
index 78e7861c6..4be9d3221 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/aw882308.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/aw882308.c
@@ -239,6 +239,12 @@ static const struct snd_soc_dai_ops aw882308_dai_ops = {
 	.set_fmt = aw882308_set_fmt,
 	.mute_stream = aw882308_mute,
 	.no_capture_mute = 1,
+	/*
+	 * The amps lock their PLL to BCLK. AudioReach starts the back-end
+	 * graph, and so BCLK, in the CPU DAI trigger, after prepare, so
+	 * unmute (and start) from trigger, once the CPU DAI has run.
+	 */
+	.mute_unmute_on_trigger = 1,
 };
 
 static struct snd_soc_dai_driver aw882308_dai = {
